<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name "StorageGuard">
<!ENTITY author "RifleJock">
<!ENTITY version "2026.08.17aa">
<!ENTITY launch "Settings/StorageGuard">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ibigsnet/StorageGuard/main/storageguard.plg">
<!ENTITY github "ibigsnet/StorageGuard">
<!ENTITY raw "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ibigsnet/StorageGuard/main">
<!ENTITY plugdir "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/StorageGuard">
<!ENTITY configdir "/boot/config/plugins/StorageGuard">
<!ENTITY pkg "StorageGuard-&version;-x86_64-1">
<!ENTITY pkgfile "&pkg;.txz">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;"
  author="&author;"
  version="&version;"
  launch="&launch;"
  pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
  icon="shield"
  min="6.12.0"
  support="https://forums.unraid.net/topic/199796-plugin-storage-guard-free-space-thresholds-so-you-know-if-a-failed-disk-still-leaves-room-to-move-data/"
  project="https://github.com/&github;"
  readme="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main/README.md">

<CHANGES>
###&version;
- <strong>Stock UI inject harden:</strong> only edits fixed Unraid HeadInlineJS paths (never walks
  the array or folders named “Storage Guard”). Marker-only strip; one-time stock backup on flash;
  uninstall removes the marker block only. SECURITY.md matches full flash wipe.

###2026.08.16ac
- <strong>Install/upgrade:</strong> always removepkg prior StorageGuard-* packages and wipe
  emhttp plugin dir before the new .txz (no mixed leftover files after versioned updates).

###2026.08.16ab
- <strong>Array defaults:</strong> Warning = largest data disk, Critical = smallest data disk;
  Array Warning <em>and</em> Critical alerts on (new install / Default / first open). Saved configs
  unchanged until Default or re-Apply.

###2026.08.16aa
- <strong>Capacity labels = Unraid Main (decimal SI):</strong> disk-size dropdowns show e.g.
  <strong>25.9T</strong> like Main Size, not binary TiB as 23.6T. Legacy binary labels remap when
  they still match a live disk.

###2026.08.15af
- **Uninstall:** remove all plugin-owned flash config and runtime scratch (clean reinstall).
- Wipe StorageGuard.cfg and /tmp/storageguard_alerts on remove.

###2026.08.15ae
- Fix: do not wipe Unraid /tmp/plugins working copy during install prepare.

###2026.08.14ae
- **Pool thresholds flexible:** Warning/Critical = free-space severity (yellow/red), not hard-wired
  to largest/smallest disk. Saved Custom or disk-size values win; empty soft-defaults to capacity-fit
  suggestions. Suggest recommends largest-loss Δ → Warning, smallest-loss Δ → Critical (user may reverse).
- Clearer pool notification text; guide + alternate scenarios: docs/math/threshold-guide.md.

###2026.08.14ad
- **Pool free thresholds (capacity-fit):** Warning = free needed so data still fits after
  <em>largest</em> member loss; Critical = after <em>smallest</em> member loss (equal disks share
  one floor). Paint/alerts use this for RAID1/1cN/RAID10/RAID5/6 unless Custom. Drops 2× rebalance pad.
- Docs: scenarios, RAID1, RAID10, math README updated.

###2026.08.14ac
- **Fix:** pools-only / no array — product Default and first open no longer enable Array coloring
  or Array Warning alerts; Array UI stays hidden (Show hidden items…). default.cfg documents
  machine-aware defaults; sg-update.php sets array_coloring / alerts from live disks.ini.

###2026.08.14ab
- Support link points at Unraid forum thread (topic 199796); project remains GitHub.
- **Lab channel:** On branch `main`, PluginURL + raw FILE sources point at `main` (lab uninstall/reinstall testing).
- Branch `stable` remains the CA/production pin Production channel is branch `stable` (CA PluginURL).

###2026.08.14aa
- **License:** GNU GPLv3 or later (copyright ibigs, LLC; Author: RifleJock). MIT retired for new releases.
- **Release channel:** PluginURL + raw FILE sources pin to GitHub branch `stable` (not `main`). Develop on `main`; ship by merging to `stable`.
- CA templates and install URLs follow `stable` for store users.

### Older releases
- Full changelog (all versions): https://github.com/ibigsnet/StorageGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
echo "StorageGuard: preparing..."
# Note: do not delete /tmp/plugins/storageguard.plg here — Unraid install working copy
mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/StorageGuard
# YYYY.MM.DDxx package names: always remove prior installs so upgrades never leave mixed files
for p in /var/log/packages/StorageGuard-*; do
  [ -e "$p" ] || continue
  echo "StorageGuard: removing old package $(basename "$p")"
  removepkg "$(basename "$p")" 2>/dev/null || true
done
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/StorageGuard \
       /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/storageguard 2>/dev/null || true
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/StorageGuard/StorageGuard-*.txz 2>/dev/null || true
echo "StorageGuard: ready."
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/StorageGuard/&pkgfile;" Run="upgradepkg --install-new --reinstall">
<URL>&raw;/archive/&pkgfile;?v=&version;</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
echo "StorageGuard: finishing install..."
if [ ! -f /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/StorageGuard/sg-lib.php ]; then
  echo "StorageGuard: ERROR — package did not install (missing sg-lib.php)"
  exit 1
fi
VER=""
for candidate in /tmp/plugins/storageguard.plg /boot/config/plugins/storageguard.plg; do
  if [ -f "$candidate" ]; then
    VER=$(sed -n 's/.*ENTITY version "\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p' "$candidate" | head -1)
    [ -n "$VER" ] && break
  fi
done
[ -z "$VER" ] && VER="unknown"
mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/StorageGuard
if [ ! -f /boot/config/plugins/StorageGuard/StorageGuard.cfg ] \
   && [ -f /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/StorageGuard/default.cfg ]; then
  cp -a /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/StorageGuard/default.cfg /boot/config/plugins/StorageGuard/StorageGuard.cfg
fi
# Main free-bar CSS/JS: ONLY these Unraid layout files (absolute paths).
# Never walks /mnt, shares, or any folder named "Storage Guard".
# Marker-only strip (no broad "Storage Guard" text match).
SG_MARKER='StorageGuard-inject'
SG_BACKUP=/boot/config/plugins/StorageGuard/stock-backup
mkdir -p "$SG_BACKUP"
sg_strip_inject() {
  local f="$1"
  [ -f "$f" ] || return 0
  # Drop our marker block + legacy inject lines (plugin asset paths only)
  sed -i \
    -e "/${SG_MARKER}/d" \
    -e '/storageguard-color\.js/d' \
    -e '/storageguard\.css/d' \
    -e '/plugins\/StorageGuard\/storageguard/d' \
    "$f" 2>/dev/null || true
}
for f in \
  /usr/local/emhttp/webGui/include/DefaultPageLayout/HeadInlineJS.php \
  /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/dynamix/include/DefaultPageLayout/HeadInlineJS.php
do
  [ -f "$f" ] || continue
  base=$(basename "$f")
  if [ ! -f "$SG_BACKUP/$base.stock" ]; then
    cp -a "$f" "$SG_BACKUP/$base.stock"
    echo "StorageGuard: backed up stock $base"
  fi
  sg_strip_inject "$f"
done
HI="/usr/local/emhttp/webGui/include/DefaultPageLayout/HeadInlineJS.php"
if [ -f "$HI" ]; then
  {
    printf '\n<!-- %s begin -->\n' "$SG_MARKER"
    printf '<link rel="stylesheet" href="/plugins/StorageGuard/storageguard.css?v=%s">\n' "$VER"
    printf '<script src="/plugins/StorageGuard/storageguard-color.js?v=%s"></script>\n' "$VER"
    printf '<!-- %s end -->\n' "$SG_MARKER"
  } >> "$HI"
  echo "StorageGuard: injected into HeadInlineJS (marker ${SG_MARKER})"
fi
echo "StorageGuard: packages now: $(ls /var/log/packages/StorageGuard-* 2>/dev/null | xargs -n1 basename 2>/dev/null | tr '\n' ' ')"
echo "StorageGuard: install complete. Hard-refresh the browser (Ctrl+Shift+R)."
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
echo "StorageGuard: removing..."
# Strip inject from fixed layout paths only — never array/share paths
SG_MARKER='StorageGuard-inject'
for f in \
  /usr/local/emhttp/webGui/include/DefaultPageLayout/HeadInlineJS.php \
  /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/dynamix/include/DefaultPageLayout/HeadInlineJS.php \
  /usr/local/emhttp/webGui/include/HeadInclude.php \
  /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/dynamix/include/HeadInclude.php
do
  [ -f "$f" ] || continue
  sed -i \
    -e "/${SG_MARKER}/d" \
    -e '/storageguard-color\.js/d' \
    -e '/storageguard\.css/d' \
    -e '/plugins\/StorageGuard\/storageguard/d' \
    "$f" 2>/dev/null || true
done
for p in /var/log/packages/StorageGuard-*; do
  [ -e "$p" ] || continue
  removepkg "$(basename "$p")" 2>/dev/null || true
done
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/StorageGuard
# Full uninstall: flash config + stock backups + runtime scratch (clean reinstall)
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/StorageGuard
rm -rf /tmp/storageguard_alerts
rm -f /tmp/plugins/storageguard.txt 2>/dev/null || true
# Note: do not delete /tmp/plugins/storageguard.plg here — Unraid install working copy
# Note: do not touch /boot/config/plugins-removed/ (Unraid-owned)
# Note: does not touch user shares, /mnt, or folders named "Storage Guard"
echo "StorageGuard: removed."
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
